## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-tenant observability with strict data isolation, covering tracing, logging, sampling, and validation.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry and trace propagation
- Tenant isolation and boundary enforcement
- Per-tenant sampling and data redaction
- Validation in a single-namespace scenario

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII redaction example (logs)
function redactLogEvent(event, tenantId) {
  const safe = {...event};
  if (safe.message) safe.message = safe.message.replace(/\b(email|ssn|password)\b[^:]*: [^,]+/gi, 'PII_REDACTED');
  if (safe.user && safe.user.id) safe.user.id = 'REDACTED';
  return safe;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and remediate cross-tenant leakage in traces?
- What metrics would you surface to confirm per-tenant isolation is preserved during incidents?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical integration of image provenance with runtime attestation, ensuring defense in depth for CNF deployments in multi-region clusters.

## Key Concepts
- Image signing with Cosign and KMS-backed keys
- SPDX SBOM association and SBOM validation
- In-cluster attestation service generating verifiable tokens
- Admission control enforcing both provenance and attestation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: basic attestation gate
function attest(imageDigest, token, sbom) {
  if (!verifySignature(imageDigest)) return false;
  if (!verifySBOM(sbom)) return false;
  if (!verifyToken(token)) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle key rotation and revocation in the KMS?
- How would you simulate attestation failures in a namespace to verify policy behavior?
